## Sources & references

The value creation / value capture distinction is foundational in strategy literature; the cleanest treatment is Michael Porter's *Competitive Advantage* (1985) and the body of work building on it. The "industry decides the centre of gravity" framing borrows from contingency-theory thinking and from Cedric Chin's writing at [Commoncog](https://commoncog.com) on how operating dynamics differ across business types. Hamilton Helmer's *7 Powers* (2016), which Part 3.1 will use directly, articulates the durability question this article ends on. Specific pay ranges in the worked example are illustrative based on 2025–2026 Malaysian recruitment market data (Robert Walters, Hays, JobStreet salary surveys), which the reader should verify before using as benchmarks.
